nu-item menu-item-type-post_type menu-item-object-page menu-item-15064"><a href="https://phxinjurylaw.com/tools/" class="nitro-lazy"><span class="link-inner">Tools</span></a></li> </ul> </li> <li id="menu-item-15065" class="menu-item menu-item-type-post_type menu-item-object-page menu-item-15065"><a href="https://phxinjurylaw.com/contact-us/"><span class="link-inner">CONTACT US</span></a></li> <li id="menu-item-15066" class="menu-item menu-item-type-post_type menu-item-object-page menu-item-15066"><a href="https://phxinjurylaw.com/blog/"><span class="link-inner">BLOG</span></a></li> </ul></nav> </div> </header> <main id="main" class="site-main wpex-clr"> <div id="content-wrap" class="container wpex-clr"> <div id="primary" class="content-area wpex-clr"> <div id="content" class="site-content wpex-clr"> <div class="custom-singular-template entry wpex-clr"><div style="background-image:url(&quot;data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIABAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAEALAAAAAABAAEAAAICTAEAOw==&quot;) !important;min-height:25%;" class="vc_row wpb_row vc_row-fluid pageRow vc_custom_1723581655113 vc_row-o-content-middle vc_row-flex wpex-vc_row-has-fill wpex-vc-reset-negative-margin wpex-has-overlay wpex-relative wpex-vc-full-width-row wpex-vc-full-width-row--centered nitro-lazy" nitro-lazy-bg="https://phxinjurylaw.com/nitropack_static/PsIVlnPjMRFbchgJxwHlSaLgBrWiMyPr/assets/images/optimized/rev-3a12724/phxinjurylaw.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/unnamed-4.png"><div class="wpex-bg-overlay-wrap wpex-absolute wpex-inset-0 wpex-rounded-inherit"><span class="wpex-bg-overlay color wpex-absolute wpex-inset-0 wpex-rounded-inherit wpex-opacity-60 wpex-bg-black" style="background-color:#1f345e;"></span></div><div class="wpb_column vc_column_container vc_col-sm-12"><div class="vc_column-inner"><div class="wpb_wrapper"><div class="vcex-page-title vcex-module wpex-text-center vc_custom_1723832250226 mainTemplateTitle vcex_690f8abc6f3af"><h1 class="vcex-page-title__heading wpex-heading wpex-text-3xl"><span class="vcex-page-title__text">Phoenix Bone Fracture Lawyer</span></h1></div><div class="vc_custom_1740081071352 wpex-clr"><div class="theme-button-wrap textcenter wpex-clr"><a href="tel:4806808125" class="vcex-button theme-button align-center inline" style="background:#ffac33;padding-top:0px;padding-bottom:0px;color:#333;font-size:23px;font-weight:600;" data-wpex-hover='{&quot;background&quot;:&quot;#ffbd5b&quot;,&quot;color&quot;:&quot;#333333&quot;}'><span class="vcex-button-inner theme-button-inner">Call Now (480) 680-8125</span></a></div></div> </div></div></div></div><div class="vc_row wpb_row vc_row-fluid mainContentWrapper vc_custom_1723588784365 wpex-vc_row-has-fill wpex-vc-reset-negative-margin" style="z-index:99 !important;"><div class="wpb_column vc_column_container vc_col-sm-12"><div class="vc_column-inner"><div class="wpb_wrapper"> <div class="vcex-post-content"> <div class="vcex-post-content-c wpex-clr"> <p>Broken bone injuries are often severe and may require extensive medical care. These injuries may also require months or years of rehabilitation. If the injury was caused by the negligent or intentional acts of another person, victims could seek the assistance of a bone fracture lawyer from Phoenix Accident and Injury Law Firm to take legal action and seek compensation for injuries sustained as a result of the accident.<br />Don&#8217;t let a broken bone injury hold you back. Contact <a href="https://phxinjurylaw.com/">Phoenix Accident and Injury Law</a> today for a free consultation, and let our bone fracture lawyers help you get the justice you deserve.</p> <h2><img fetchpriority="high" alt="She needs a bone fracture lawyer." width="700" height="247" nitro-lazy-src="https://phxinjurylaw.com/nitropack_static/PsIVlnPjMRFbchgJxwHlSaLgBrWiMyPr/assets/images/optimized/rev-3a12724/phxinjuryl1dev.wpenginepowered.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/unnamed-5-300x106.png" class="aligncenter wp-image-15969 nitro-lazy" decoding="async" nitro-lazy-empty id="MzE2OjI0Nw==-1" src="data:image/svg+xml;nitro-empty-id=MzE2OjI0Nw==-1;base64,PHN2ZyB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMzAwIDEwNiIgd2lkdGg9IjMwMCIgaGVpZ2h0PSIxMDYiIHhtbG5zPSJodHRwOi8vd3d3LnczLm9yZy8yMDAwL3N2ZyI+PC9zdmc+" /></h2> <h2>Understanding Broken Bones and Fractures</h2> <p>Broken bones are common injuries related to motor vehicles, motorcycles, pedestrians, and workplace accidents. Almost everyone is likely to experience a broken bone at some point in their life. However, broken bones and fractures are severe and incredibly painful injuries that require immediate medical treatment, even if they can be a frequent occurrence.</p> <p>Most broken bone injuries are life-altering and can leave victims with life-disrupting disabilities either temporarily or permanently. A victim with a broken bone may not be able to return to work or even perform simple daily activities. The complicated healing nature of wounds makes them especially dangerous for young children and the elderly.</p> <p>Generally, broken bones and fractures require lengthy rehabilitation and expensive medical treatment. However, you can recover damages for broken bone injuries due to someone else&#8217;s negligence. If you or someone you know has suffered a broken bone due to another party&#8217;s negligence, a bone fracture lawyer from Phoenix Accident and Injury Law can help you seek compensation for your injuries and losses. Our experienced broken bones attorney are dedicated to fighting for your rights and ensuring you receive the fair treatment you deserve.</p> <h3>Common Causes of Bone Injuries in Arizona</h3> <p>Our bone fracture lawyer has represented injury victims who have suffered broken or fractured bones in the following scenarios:</p> <ul> <li>Vehicle, motorcycle, and truck collisions</li> <li>Workplace accidents</li> <li>Slip and fall accidents</li> <li>Construction accidents</li> <li>Injuries caused by defective products</li> <li>Bicycle or pedestrian accidents</li> <li>Domestic abuse environments</li> <li>Boating accidents</li> <li>Animal attacks</li> <li>Nursing home abuse</li> </ul> <p><br />People with broken bones or fractures<a href="https://phxinjurylaw.com/practice-areas/fractured-bones-in-a-car-accident/"> can seek compensation</a> from the responsible parties with the help of our bone fracture lawyer. We believe that you should be compensated if the harm you suffered was the result of someone else&#8217;s reckless behavior.</p> <h3>Types of Bone Fractures and Their Impact</h3> <p>Fractures and broken bones are common injuries in Phoenix, AZ, often resulting from another party&#8217;s negligence. Here are some types of fractures our bone fracture lawyer usually encounters:</p> <p><br /><strong>Complete fractures</strong>: A classic &#8220;broken bone&#8221; where the bone snaps into two pieces.</p> <p><strong>Comminuted fractures</strong>: A more severe fracture where the bone breaks into three or more pieces.</p> <p><strong>Hairline fractures</strong>: Also known as &#8220;stress fractures,&#8221; these are tiny cracks in the bone.</p> <p><strong>Stable fractures</strong>: The bone cracks but does not shift out of place.</p> <p><strong>Displaced fractures</strong>: The bone cracks and shifts out of alignment.</p> <p><strong>Incomplete fractures</strong>: The bone does not break entirely apart.</p> <p><strong>Compound or open fractures</strong>: A severe fracture where the bone punctures the skin.</p> <p><strong>Transverse fractures</strong>: A break that occurs horizontally.</p> <p><strong>Oblique fractures</strong>: A break that occurs diagonally.</p> <p><strong>Simple fractures</strong>: A general term for various types of fractures, including comminuted, impacted, oblique, transverse, and hairline fractures.</p> <p><strong>Spiral fractures</strong>: A break that follows a twisting pattern, often caused by slips and falls.</p> <p><strong>Greenstick fractures</strong>: A fracture that occurs in a bone that hasn&#8217;t fully hardened, causing it to bend and crack but remain in one piece.</p> <p><strong>Segmental fractures</strong>: A fracture where a bone breaks into two or more pieces, and one piece is disconnected from the others.</p> <p><strong>Any of these fractures can have a significant impact on your life. </strong>A broken bone injury can disrupt your daily routine, limit your mobility, and affect your ability to work or participate in activities you enjoy.</p> <p><br /><strong>If you&#8217;ve suffered a<a href="https://phxinjurylaw.com/blog/broken-bones-in-a-car-accident/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"> broken bone</a> due to someone else&#8217;s negligence, you may be entitled to compensation.</strong> Our bone fracture lawyer can help you understand your legal rights and pursue the compensation you deserve.</p> <h2>The Legal Process for Broken Bone Claims in Phoenix</h2> <h3>Navigating the Claims Process</h3> <p>When you&#8217;ve suffered a broken bone due to another party&#8217;s negligence, it&#8217;s essential to seek legal advice promptly. At Phoenix Accident and Injury Law, our bone fracture lawyer is committed to providing you with the expert representation you need.</p> <p><strong>Here&#8217;s how we can help:</strong></p> <p><strong>Free Case Evaluation:</strong> We&#8217;ll review your case at no cost to determine if you have a valid claim.</p> <p><strong>Thorough Investigation:</strong> Our team will gather evidence, including photos, medical records, and witness statements, to build a strong case.</p> <p><strong>Calculation of Damages:</strong> We&#8217;ll carefully calculate your financial losses, including medical expenses, lost wages, and pain and suffering.</p> <p><strong>Demand Letter:</strong> We&#8217;ll draft a demand letter to the responsible party&#8217;s insurance company, outlining your claim and negotiating a fair settlement.</p> <p><strong>Litigation:</strong> If necessary, we&#8217;ll represent you in court and fight aggressively to protect your rights.</p> <p>Contact our <strong>bone fracture lawyer</strong> for a free consultation on your case.</p> <h3>Understanding the Statute of Limitations in Arizona</h3> <p>Time is of the essence. <a href="https://www.azleg.gov/ars/12/00542.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Arizona&#8217;s statute of limitations</a> typically gives you two years from the date of your injury to file a claim. Don&#8217;t delay. Contact us today for a free consultation with our bone fracture lawyer.</p> <h2>Work-Related Broken Bone Injuries</h2> <h3>Filing Workers&#8217; Compensation Claims for Bone Fractures</h3> <p>After a workplace injury, it&#8217;s crucial to report the incident to your supervisor promptly and file a workers&#8217; compensation claim. Our bone fracture lawyer at Phoenix Accident and Injury Law can guide you through this process and ensure you receive the maximum benefits possible.<br />Our bone fracture attorney will work closely with you to gather evidence, navigate the medical evaluation process, and negotiate with the insurance company for a fair settlement. Our goal is to help you secure the compensation you deserve for your injuries and lost wages.</p> <p><strong>Don&#8217;t delay. Contact our bone fracture lawyer today for a free consultation.</strong></p> <h2>Compensation for Broken Bone Injuries</h2> <h3>Types of Compensation Available</h3> <p>When you suffer a broken bone due to another party&#8217;s negligence, a bone fracture lawyer can get you compensation for both economic and non-economic damages.</p> <p><strong>Economic damages</strong> include quantifiable losses such as:</p> <ul> <li>Medical expenses</li> <li>Lost wages</li> <li>Property damage</li> </ul> <p><strong>Non-economic damages</strong> are intangible losses, including:</p> <ul> <li>Pain and suffering</li> <li>Emotional distress</li> <li>Disability</li> </ul> <p>At Phoenix Accident and Injury Law, our bone fracture lawyers are dedicated to helping you recover the total compensation you deserve. We&#8217;ll work tirelessly to calculate your damages and negotiate with the insurance company for a fair settlement.</p> <h2>Client Testimonials and Success Stories</h2> <h3>Hear From Our Satisfied Clients</h3> <p>“This law firm is compassionate and efficient. They keep you updated throughout the entire process, and their staff goes beyond expectations!”</p> <p><a href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/TkTGo7a3pvC31LdRA" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read full review</a></p> <h2>Contact Our Expert Broken Bone Injury Lawyers</h2> <h3>Free Legal Consultation for Broken Bone Victims</h3> <p>At Phoenix Accident and Injury Law, our bone fracture lawyer is dedicated to fighting for your rights and ensuring you receive the compensation you deserve after a severe injury. We understand the physical and emotional challenges that broken bones can present, and we&#8217;re here to provide the support and legal representation you need.<br />Our experienced broken bone lawyer will work tirelessly to gather evidence, build a strong case, and negotiate with the insurance company for a fair settlement. We&#8217;re committed to helping you recover the maximum compensation possible so you can focus on your recovery and move forward with your life.</p> <h2>Contact Information and Office Locations</h2> <p>At Phoenix Accident and Injury Law firm, we serve clients throughout Arizona, with offices in Chandler, Gilbert, Mesa, Scottsdale, Tempe, and Peoria. <a href="https://phxinjurylaw.com/contact-us/">Contact us</a> today for a free consultation.</p></div> </div> </div></div></div></div><div class="vc_row wpb_row vc_row-fluid vc_custom_1723588833833 wpex-vc_row-has-fill wpex-vc-reset-negative-margin wpex-vc-full-width-row wpex-vc-full-width-row--centered"><div class="wpb_column vc_column_container vc_col-sm-12"><div class="vc_column-inner"><div class="wpb_wrapper"><div class="wpex-template-shortcode"><div class="vc_row wpb_row vc_row-fluid vc_row-o-equal-height vc_row-flex"><div class="wpb_column vc_column_container vc_col-